00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:06.660
But in this case, it
happened with other people.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.290
What did happen here is--

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.630
let me go back in this one.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:16.440
I mean, you know, besides
like, you know, if I move now,

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.280
you will be moving.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.488
If you move I will be moving.

00:19:18.488 --> 00:19:22.740
And then this kind of
sharing of the space

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:25.680
or the possibility to move
and be moved by somebody

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.700
who you don't expect.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.880
But I think so the more
it kind of funny part

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.000
is like when somebody entering
the lower part in the entrance,

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.190
well, it's a big
pressurized space.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.320
I mean, when you enter
in the lower space,

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:42.570
you know, you've got a
very, very strong wind

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.460
which comes to you, and somehow,
you don't know what happened.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.720
But the people which are on
top, they say, close the door!

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:54.587
Because everything collapse the
system very quickly situation.

00:19:54.587 --> 00:19:56.670
There is, again, you know,
there is the engagement

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.570
between the people which are
kind of on different levels,

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:02.340
but also with the
people which enter.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.820
And somehow you don't realize
that how much the things are

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:09.957
related, but somehow it works.

00:20:09.957 --> 00:20:12.540
And then the other thing, which
was kind of a nightmare, also,

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:18.990
is try to get the approval
of how to get it there.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.960
Because, I mean, three layers,
when you put a lot of pressure

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:26.100
in the cube, which is 7,000
cubic meters of air, all

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.450
the three layers are squeezed.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.800
I mean, I just explained.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.840
I mean, I don't have a
better method of what--

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:32.250
lasagna, maybe.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.250
I start to get angry.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.770
But, you know, there is no
space in between all of them.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.150
This means when you
enter with your own body,

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.560
you kind of open the space.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.440
And as big as you are, or if
you enter between two person,

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.850
then you kind of bend the space.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:47.460
You know, which drive kind
of a very simple relationship

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.160
with the theory of
relativity, of how much

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.440
you have a mass of
body somehow, all

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:56.640
people or planets will be kind
of bond one to each other.

00:20:56.640 --> 00:21:00.060
But the more complicated
was to try to speculate that

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:01.110
if it gonna work or not.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:04.960
Because when you have somebody
on top, for example, going to

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:05.460
squeeze.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.000
Doesn't mean you have to
move to the other level.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.490
And when you are here,
you squeeze the other one

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:09.300
which is below.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.400
This means there is a
lot of synchronicity

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:16.320
between how people moves
and how much is affected.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.080
I mean, I'm passionate
about the butterfly effect

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.890
and how we might relate
one to each other.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:23.910
Yeah, here.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.470
People up here.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.270
I will not go back to that one.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:32.130
But, well, this is a
drawing by Paul Davies

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:36.078
when he tried to talk
about spacetime foam more

00:21:36.078 --> 00:21:36.870
on a quantic scale.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.550
And, you know,
it's still kind of,

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:41.100
it is a dimension which
kind of fascinate me.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:47.880
I try to understand it and maybe
to reinterpret in some way.

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:51.180
I mean, here is also, these
guys pretty much in trouble,

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:54.630
because they cannot go
out from the installation.

00:21:58.035 --> 00:22:00.270
Again, there is a
lot of security,

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:01.590
which we try to avoid it.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.320
But for these men to
go out, somebody else

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.310
has to go to the bottom
of the installation.

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:08.850
And then he will be lift up,
and then he can get a staircase

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:12.000
and go out.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.810
It take a while, it'll
be, until you learn.

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:20.010
And then another thing which
happened, usually, I mean, I'm

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:24.570
pretty much, at the beginning,
when I was doing installation,

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:27.270
we tried to make a
manual of how to use it.

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:29.580
Because it kind of is
a constant learning

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:32.190
process for me and for the
people who somehow have to take

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:32.690
care.

00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:35.580
But another thing
is, people usually

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.127
like to be together in a space.

00:22:37.127 --> 00:22:39.210
But when you be together
in a space, it's kind of,

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.800
you really go deep.

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:42.900
Much more than these.

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:46.580
It's very difficult to escape
from these kind of black holes

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:48.450
situation.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:49.043
There we are.

00:22:49.043 --> 00:22:51.210
That was the first time
that I entered kind of alone

00:22:51.210 --> 00:22:52.918
and this guy tried to
come and rescue me.

00:22:52.918 --> 00:22:57.160
But I didn't disappear here.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.980
Anyway, one of the
idea, and I think

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:02.970
it's also when I received
the invitation of MIT,

00:23:02.970 --> 00:23:05.370
which somehow was a dream,
