00:56:15.660 --> 00:56:17.850
By the presence of
that structure that

00:56:17.850 --> 00:56:22.620
constructs and somehow generates
a landscape that conditions,

00:56:22.620 --> 00:56:26.400
that constrains, experience,
the way you inhabit it.

00:56:26.400 --> 00:56:29.190
In the project in
Milan, you were

00:56:29.190 --> 00:56:33.150
talking about the full social
experience of rebalancing,

00:56:33.150 --> 00:56:39.060
of close the door, because
that different of pressure

00:56:39.060 --> 00:56:41.260
was generating the
movement of people.

00:56:43.830 --> 00:56:47.790
There's a full narrative
in that scientific process.

00:56:47.790 --> 00:56:48.290
Yeah.

00:56:52.252 --> 00:56:54.210
When I think it's like,
what the hell is space?

00:56:54.210 --> 00:56:55.320
You know, I don't know.

00:56:55.320 --> 00:56:57.670
That's the only problem
that I stop even before.

00:56:57.670 --> 00:56:58.170
You know?

00:56:58.170 --> 00:57:00.090
It's like, and then
I read string theory,

00:57:00.090 --> 00:57:04.440
