00:57:58.630 --> 00:58:02.010
I'm fascinating about the
idea that you enter up here,

00:58:02.010 --> 00:58:04.020
and you open it.

00:58:04.020 --> 00:58:05.310
You open this space.

00:58:05.310 --> 00:58:08.070
And then you move up here
and the space follows you.

00:58:08.070 --> 00:58:10.410
I mean, that's, for me,
in architectural terms,

00:58:10.410 --> 00:58:11.550
is fantastic.

00:58:11.550 --> 00:58:15.090
It's a a space who does not
exist, that with my body,

00:58:15.090 --> 00:58:19.270
it opened a space very,
very kind of perfect.

00:58:19.270 --> 00:58:21.000
I don't want more
space than the one

00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:22.680
that I need with my own weight.

00:58:22.680 --> 00:58:24.540
Does it mean I open
it up, the space

00:58:24.540 --> 00:58:27.510
follows me like a science
fiction movie [INAUDIBLE]..

00:58:27.510 --> 00:58:29.107
I go and I'm like, oh, my god.

00:58:29.107 --> 00:58:29.940
You know, it's like.

00:58:29.940 --> 00:58:32.910
And then I think so
that I can open a space.

00:58:32.910 --> 00:58:33.870
Oh, fancy enough.

00:58:33.870 --> 00:58:36.270
Now come these guys,
and I close my space,

00:58:36.270 --> 00:58:38.100
